From cdf0de1f34e91150e90d021a0a249e11276253e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Petr=20=C5=A0tetiar?= <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 18:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nl80211: remove the other loaded hostapd ifaces before the
 main iface on a radio re-add
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() implements the "re-add radio config"
fallback (SECDMN_ACTION_OK_NEED_RE_ADD in src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c,
taken by s_doRemoveLink() whenever hostapd does not offer LINK_REMOVE
and by s_removeBss() when the target is the main VAP) with a single
global "REMOVE <main VAP socket name>", after which
wld_rad_hostapd_addConf() re-adds the radio config listing every enabled
VAP of the radio.

That assumes all VAPs of the radio are BSSes of the main VAP's
hostapd_iface, so that the one REMOVE tears down the whole radio. With
hostapd 2024.09 ("AP MLD: Allow new link to be added through control
interface") this no longer holds for AP MLD links: in
hostapd_interface_init_bss() (src/ap/hostapd.c) an "ADD bss_config="
whose BSS has mld_ap=1 always gets a hostapd_iface of its own, even when
an iface with the same phy label exists. Since pWHM warm-adds each VAP
with its own per-BSS config (s_doAddLink() -> wld_ap_hostapd_addBssConf()),
a 6 GHz radio hosting wlan0.1 (link of MLD wlan2.1), wlan0.2 (link of
MLD wlan2.2) and wlan0.3 ends up as three hostapd_ifaces with phy label
"wlan0".

Observed on a mac80211 AP MLD setup (three MLDs across three radios)
during Freedom 100-pwhm_step_2.t, first step AccessPoint.9.Enable=0
(wlan0.3, non-Tx BSS):

  wlan0.3: disabling non Tx BSS, scheduling re-add link of Tx bss wlan0.1
  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan2.1_link2'          <- wlan0.1's iface only
  hostapd: wlan2.1_link2: interface state ENABLED->DISABLED  (one BSS)
  hostapd: Configuration file: /tmp/wlan0_hapd.conf (phy wlan0)  (no "new PHY")
  hostapd: wlan2.1: interface state UNINITIALIZED->COUNTRY_UPDATE
  hostapd: MLD: Failed to add link 3 in MLD wlan2.2
  hostapd: Interface initialization failed

wlan0.2's hostapd_iface (socket wlan2.2_link2) and its kernel link 2 on
netdev wlan2.2 stay registered; the re-added radio config carries wlan0.2
again with the same bssid, hostapd allocates MLD link id 3 for it and the
kernel refuses NL80211_CMD_ADD_LINK (mac80211
ieee80211_check_dup_link_addrs(), duplicate link address on the same
netdev: -EALREADY by source, hostapd logs the errno only at MSG_DEBUG).
AccessPoint.9 never reports Disabled ("enable=0 timed out"). The next
step (AccessPoint.8.Enable=0, 5 GHz) repeats it with "Failed to add link
4 in MLD wlan2.2" because wlan1.2's iface is alive too, that ADD fails
synchronously and s_doAddHostapd() escalates to "warm apply failed to add
iface conf => restart to recover": the whole shared hostapd is restarted.
The same trigger in 101-mlo_step_2.t passed because there the wlan0
BSSes were plain BSSes of one hostapd_iface (hostapd logged
wlan0.1/wlan0.2/wlan0.3 AP-DISABLED for the single REMOVE and "--> new
PHY" on the ADD).

The layout is not fixed either: after such a re-add the full radio
config goes in as one "ADD bss_config=", so the main VAP is bss[0] and
the other MLD links are bss[1..] of one hostapd_iface, while VAPs
warm-added later get ifaces of their own again. Both layouts, and
mixtures of them, have to be removed correctly.

Fix: remove every hostapd_iface holding a loaded BSS of the radio, each
one addressed by its own first BSS (bss[0]), with the recipe already
used for the main iface: "SET interface <sockname>" on the BSS socket
when the socket name is not the bare ifname (MLD link sockets are
"<iface>_link<N>" and hostapd_remove_iface() matches the configured
interface name of bss[0]), then the global "REMOVE <sockname>", which
runs the whole-iface teardown and thereby removes the kernel MLD links
of all its BSSes (hostapd_cleanup_driver() -> hostapd_if_link_remove()
for bss[0], hostapd_free_hapd_data() for the started others). A
secondary BSS must not be addressed itself: hostapd's "SET interface"
rewrites the interface name of bss[0] of the iface holding the addressed
BSS, exactly like the "interface=" config line (hostapd_config_fill(),
hostapd/config_file.c: os_strlcpy(conf->bss[0]->iface, ...)), so the
recipe applied to a secondary BSS renames and removes the owner's iface
and the later step on the owner's socket fails on a dead socket:

  wlan0.2: disabling non Tx BSS, scheduling re-add link of Tx bss wlan0.1
  hostapd: Remove interface 'wlan2.2_link3'    <- the main VAP wlan0.1, renamed
  hostapd: wlan2.2_link3: interface state ENABLED->DISABLED
  hostapd: wlan2.2: AP-DISABLED                <- bss[1] = wlan0.2
  hostapd: wlan2.2_link3: AP-DISABLED          <- bss[0] = wlan0.1
  wld: wlan0: fail to restore iface name (wlan0.1->wlan2.1_link3)
  wld: wlan0: warm apply failed to remove iface conf => restart to recover

The iface layout is read from hostapd itself, for every loaded BSS of
the radio (its control socket exists), before any destructive command:
the "STATUS" reply on any BSS socket lists the BSSes of the iface
holding it (bss[N]=, mld_link_id[N]=, hostapd_ctrl_iface_status()), and
the control socket name of each listed BSS is rebuilt from it the way
hostapd names it (hostapd_set_ctrl_sock_iface(): "<iface>" or
"<iface>_link<mld_link_id>"). A BSS owns its iface iff the rebuilt name
of bss[0] is its own socket name; otherwise that name has to be the
socket of another loaded BSS of the radio which owns its iface, and the
addressed BSS has to appear in its own list. Only hostapd's running
identity is used: pWHM's pSSID->BSSID is already updated when a BSSID
change takes this path (the GEN_FSM_REMOVE_LINK re-add runs before
GEN_FSM_MOD_BSSID), so comparing it with hostapd's bssid[0] would
mistake a still running independent iface for a secondary BSS and leave
it loaded. The connection socket names are refreshed
(wld_wpaCtrlMngr_checkAllIfaces(), its result checked) before the
default connection is selected and before hostapd is queried, since a
BSS socket is renamed to its MLD link socket after setup; the command
wrapper uses a temporary connection when the BSS's wpactrl client is not
connected, so a loaded-but-unready BSS is classified as well.

The owners are then removed one by one, the owner of the iface holding
pWHM's default connection last (wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getDefaultInterface()
picks a ready connection, not necessarily an owner, so that owner is
resolved from the classification), which keeps the connection used by
the wpactrl manager up until the end. Secondary BSSes are skipped: they
go away with their owner's iface. A VAP whose socket is gone is not
loaded and is skipped as well.

A failed socket refresh, a STATUS that cannot be obtained or does not
list the addressed BSS under its own socket name, a bss[0] that is not a
loaded owner on this radio, a default connection that is not a loaded
BSS of the radio, and a rejected SET or REMOVE all make the function
fail, so that s_doRemoveHostapd() runs its existing recovery (hostapd
restart) instead of re-adding a config on top of a live duplicate. A
REMOVE whose reply times out is still taken as accepted, as it was for
the single main-iface REMOVE before (hostapd handles it synchronously
and the global socket is serialized); that inherited behaviour is not
changed here.

pWHM v7.29.20 is the newest source available locally and the upstream
pwhm repository could not be reached from here (HTTP 403), so the
current upstream wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf() was not compared.

Signed-off-by: Petr Štetiar <petr.stetiar@prplfoundation.org>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c | 229 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 216 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
index 74c216af9fb5..722c8f53ae03 100644
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
@@ -523,6 +523,141 @@ swl_rc_ne wld_rad_hostapd_addConf(T_Radio* pR) {
     return rc;
 }
 
+/**
+ * @brief remove one hostapd iface, addressed by the control socket name of its first BSS
+ *
+ * hostapd's global "REMOVE <name>" tears down the whole hostapd_iface whose
+ * first BSS (bss[0]) is configured with interface name <name>
+ * (hostapd_remove_iface(), src/ap/hostapd.c), including its secondary BSSes.
+ * For an AP MLD link BSS the control socket is named "<iface>_link<N>" while
+ * the configured interface name is the MLD's netdev, shared by all its links,
+ * so the interface name is first set to the socket name to make the REMOVE
+ * target unambiguous. Note that "SET interface" always rewrites the name of
+ * bss[0] of the iface owning the addressed BSS (hostapd_config_fill(),
+ * hostapd/config_file.c, same as the "interface=" config line), which is why
+ * this helper must only be used with the first BSS of an iface.
+ * The command wrapper uses a temporary connection when the wpactrl client of
+ * the BSS is not connected, so a loaded BSS is removed even while its client
+ * is unready.
+ *
+ * @param pR radio context
+ * @param pgIface hostapd global control interface
+ * @param pIface control interface of the first BSS of the iface to remove
+ *
+ * @return SWL_RC_OK when the removing cmd is accepted.
+ *         SWL_RC_CONTINUE when the command is accepted but still being processed by hostapd
+ *         Otherwise error code (also when the interface name could not be set).
+ */
+static swl_rc_ne s_removeIfaceBySockName(T_Radio* pR, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pgIface, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface) {
+    swl_rc_ne rc;
+    const char* skname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pIface);
+    const char* ifname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getName(pIface);
+    if(!swl_str_matches(skname, ifname)) {
+        rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pIface, "OK", "SET interface %s", skname);
+        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to restore iface name (%s->%s)", pR->Name, ifname, skname);
+    }
+    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pgIface, "OK", "REMOVE %s", skname);
+    //the call may timeout while being applied, but that only happens on success
+    if(rc == SWL_RC_NOT_AVAILABLE) {
+        rc = SWL_RC_CONTINUE;
+    }
+    return rc;
+}
+
+/* control socket name of a hostapd BSS: "<ifname>" or "<ifname>_link<N>" */
+#define HAPD_BSS_SOCK_NAME_LEN (IFNAMSIZ + 16)
+
+/**
+ * @brief rebuild the control socket name of the N-th BSS listed in a "STATUS" reply
+ *
+ * hostapd names the control socket of a BSS after its configured interface
+ * name (bss[N]= in the reply), suffixed with "_link<mld_link_id[N]>" for an
+ * AP MLD link BSS (hostapd_set_ctrl_sock_iface(), src/ap/hostapd.c).
+ *
+ * @param reply "STATUS" reply
+ * @param idx index N of the BSS in the reply
+ * @param skname output buffer for the socket name
+ * @param sknameSize size of the output buffer
+ *
+ * @return SWL_RC_OK when the N-th BSS is listed, SWL_RC_ERROR otherwise
+ */
+static swl_rc_ne s_getStatusBssSockName(const char* reply, uint32_t idx, char* skname, size_t sknameSize) {
+    char key[32] = {0};
+    char ifname[IFNAMSIZ + 1] = {0};
+    snprintf(key, sizeof(key), "bss[%u]", idx);
+    swl_rc_ne rc = wld_wpaCtrl_getInReplyParamValStr(reply, key, ifname, sizeof(ifname));
+    ASSERTS_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "no %s", key);
+    char linkId[8] = {0};
+    snprintf(key, sizeof(key), "mld_link_id[%u]", idx);
+    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_getInReplyParamValStr(reply, key, linkId, sizeof(linkId));
+    if(swl_rc_isOk(rc) && !swl_str_isEmpty(linkId)) {
+        snprintf(skname, sknameSize, "%s_link%s", ifname, linkId);
+    } else {
+        swl_str_copy(skname, sknameSize, ifname);
+    }
+    return SWL_RC_OK;
+}
+
+/* a BSS of the radio currently loaded in hostapd (its control socket exists) */
+typedef struct {
+    T_AccessPoint* pAP;
+    wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface;
+    /* socket name of bss[0] of the hostapd iface holding this BSS, as reported by hostapd */
+    char ownerSkname[HAPD_BSS_SOCK_NAME_LEN];
+} s_loadedBss_t;
+
+/**
+ * @brief resolve from hostapd the owner (bss[0]) of the hostapd iface holding a loaded BSS
+ *
+ * hostapd reports on the control socket of any BSS the BSS list of the
+ * hostapd_iface holding it ("STATUS" reply lines bss[N]=/bssid[N]=/
+ * mld_link_id[N]=, hostapd_ctrl_iface_status(), src/ap/ctrl_iface_ap.c),
+ * bss[0] first. bss[0] is the BSS whose interface name the global "REMOVE"
+ * matches for the whole iface and whose interface name "SET interface"
+ * rewrites. The socket names are rebuilt from that list, so the identity
+ * comes from hostapd's running state and not from pWHM's configuration
+ * (e.g. pSSID->BSSID, which is already updated while the old BSS still
+ * runs). The addressed BSS has to appear in the list under its own socket
+ * name, otherwise the reply is not trusted.
+ *
+ * @param pR radio context
+ * @param pBss the loaded BSS (pAP and pIface set), ownerSkname is filled on success
+ *
+ * @return SWL_RC_OK when the owner socket name is resolved
+ *         SWL_RC_ERROR when hostapd could not be queried or the reply is inconsistent
+ */
+static swl_rc_ne s_getLoadedBssOwner(T_Radio* pR, s_loadedBss_t* pBss) {
+    const char* skname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pBss->pIface);
+    size_t maxMsgLen = wld_wpaCtrl_getMaxMsgLen();
+    char reply[maxMsgLen];
+    memset(reply, 0, sizeof(reply));
+    swl_rc_ne rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtGetResponse(pBss->pIface, reply, sizeof(reply), "STATUS");
+    ASSERTW_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: fail to get status of bss %s (%s)", pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, skname);
+    rc = s_getStatusBssSockName(reply, 0, pBss->ownerSkname, sizeof(pBss->ownerSkname));
+    ASSERTW_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: no bss[0] in status of bss %s (%s)", pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, skname);
+    char bssSkname[HAPD_BSS_SOCK_NAME_LEN] = {0};
+    for(uint32_t i = 0; swl_rc_isOk(s_getStatusBssSockName(reply, i, bssSkname, sizeof(bssSkname))); i++) {
+        if(swl_str_matches(bssSkname, skname)) {
+            return SWL_RC_OK;
+        }
+    }
+    SAH_TRACEZ_WARNING(ME, "%s: bss %s (%s) not listed in its own status (bss[0]=%s)", pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, skname, pBss->ownerSkname);
+    return SWL_RC_ERROR;
+}
+
+static s_loadedBss_t* s_findLoadedBssBySockName(s_loadedBss_t* bsses, uint32_t nBss, const char* skname) {
+    for(uint32_t i = 0; i < nBss; i++) {
+        if(swl_str_matches(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(bsses[i].pIface), skname)) {
+            return &bsses[i];
+        }
+    }
+    return NULL;
+}
+
+static bool s_isLoadedBssOwner(s_loadedBss_t* pBss) {
+    return swl_str_matches(wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pBss->pIface), pBss->ownerSkname);
+}
+
 /**
  * @brief remove entire radio and vaps config from hostapd
  * (this will trigger removing all secondary BSSs netdev ifaces and stop radio activity)
@@ -539,23 +674,91 @@ swl_rc_ne wld_rad_hostapd_removeConf(T_Radio* pR) {
     wld_wpaCtrlMngr_t* pMgr = wld_secDmn_getWpaCtrlMgr(pR->hostapd);
     wld_secDmn_t* pSecDmn = wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getSecDmn(pMgr);
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pSecDmn, SWL_RC_INVALID_STATE, ME, "NULL");
-    wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface = wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getDefaultInterface(pMgr);
-    ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pIface, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: hostapd has no default wpactrl iface ready", pR->Name);
     wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pgIface = wld_secDmn_getGlobalCtrlIface(pSecDmn);
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pgIface, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: hostapd has no global iface ready", pR->Name);
-    swl_rc_ne rc;
-    const char* skname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pIface);
-    const char* ifname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getName(pIface);
-    if(!swl_str_matches(skname, ifname)) {
-        rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pIface, "OK", "SET interface %s", skname);
-        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to restore main iface name (%s->%s)", pR->Name, ifname, skname);
+    /*
+     * Refresh the connection socket names first (a BSS socket is renamed to
+     * its MLD link socket after setup), before anything is selected from them.
+     */
+    swl_rc_ne rc = wld_wpaCtrlMngr_checkAllIfaces(pMgr);
+    ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to check hostapd ctrl sockets", pR->Name);
+    wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pIface = wld_wpaCtrlMngr_getDefaultInterface(pMgr);
+    ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pIface, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: hostapd has no default wpactrl iface ready", pR->Name);
+
+    /*
+     * A secondary VAP added with its own "ADD bss_config=" as an AP MLD link
+     * (mld_ap=1) is not a BSS of the main VAP's hostapd iface: hostapd allocates
+     * a separate hostapd_iface for every such ADD (hostapd_interface_init_bss(),
+     * src/ap/hostapd.c, "AP MLD can be enabled with the same interface name").
+     * "REMOVE <main>" therefore leaves those VAPs, and their kernel MLD links,
+     * fully registered, and the radio config re-added right after (which lists
+     * every enabled VAP of the radio) duplicates them: the driver link add for
+     * the duplicate is refused by the kernel (same link address already present
+     * on the MLD netdev), hostapd reports "MLD: Failed to add link N in MLD X"
+     * and the warm re-add fails.
+     * So every hostapd iface holding a loaded BSS of the radio is removed, each
+     * one addressed by its own first BSS (bss[0]): addressing a secondary BSS
+     * would rename and remove the owner's iface instead (see
+     * s_removeIfaceBySockName()), e.g. all VAPs of a radio config re-added as
+     * one "ADD bss_config=" get one iface, the main VAP first. The layout is
+     * read from hostapd for every loaded BSS before any destructive command,
+     * and the iface holding pWHM's default connection is removed last. A VAP
+     * whose socket is gone is not loaded and is skipped. Any failure, or a
+     * BSS whose iface cannot be mapped to a loaded owner, aborts the removal
+     * so that the caller runs its recovery instead of re-adding a config on
+     * top of a live duplicate.
+     */
+    s_loadedBss_t bsses[MAXNROF_ACCESSPOINT];
+    memset(bsses, 0, sizeof(bsses));
+    uint32_t nBss = 0;
+    T_AccessPoint* pAP = NULL;
+    wld_rad_forEachAp(pAP, pR) {
+        wld_wpaCtrlInterface_t* pApIface = pAP->wpaCtrlInterface;
+        if((pApIface == NULL) || !wld_wpaCtrlInterface_checkConnectionPath(pApIface)) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: bss %s not loaded, skip removal", pR->Name, pAP->alias);
+            continue;
+        }
+        ASSERT_TRUE(nBss < SWL_ARRAY_SIZE(bsses), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: too many loaded bss, abort radio removal", pR->Name);
+        s_loadedBss_t* pBss = &bsses[nBss];
+        pBss->pAP = pAP;
+        pBss->pIface = pApIface;
+        rc = s_getLoadedBssOwner(pR, pBss);
+        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: unknown hostapd iface of bss %s (%s), abort radio removal",
+                    pR->Name, pAP->alias, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pApIface));
+        nBss++;
     }
-    rc = wld_wpaCtrl_sendCmdFmtCheckResponse(pgIface, "OK", "REMOVE %s", skname);
-    //the call may timeout while being applied, but that only happens on success
-    if(rc == SWL_RC_NOT_AVAILABLE) {
-        rc = SWL_RC_CONTINUE;
+    /* every loaded BSS must belong to an iface owned by a loaded BSS of the radio */
+    s_loadedBss_t* pLastBss = NULL;
+    for(uint32_t i = 0; i < nBss; i++) {
+        s_loadedBss_t* pBss = &bsses[i];
+        s_loadedBss_t* pOwner = s_findLoadedBssBySockName(bsses, nBss, pBss->ownerSkname);
+        ASSERT_TRUE((pOwner != NULL) && s_isLoadedBssOwner(pOwner), SWL_RC_ERROR, ME,
+                    "%s: bss %s (%s) is held by iface of unknown bss %s, abort radio removal",
+                    pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pBss->pIface), pBss->ownerSkname);
+        if(pBss->pIface == pIface) {
+            pLastBss = pOwner;
+        }
     }
-    return rc;
+    ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pLastBss, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "%s: default wpactrl iface (%s) is not a loaded bss of the radio, abort radio removal",
+                    pR->Name, wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pIface));
+    for(uint32_t i = 0; i < nBss; i++) {
+        s_loadedBss_t* pBss = &bsses[i];
+        const char* apSkname = wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pBss->pIface);
+        if(!s_isLoadedBssOwner(pBss)) {
+            SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: bss %s (%s) is a secondary bss of iface %s, removed with it", pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, apSkname, pBss->ownerSkname);
+            continue;
+        }
+        if(pBss == pLastBss) {
+            continue;
+        }
+        SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: remove iface of bss %s (%s)", pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, apSkname);
+        rc = s_removeIfaceBySockName(pR, pgIface, pBss->pIface);
+        ASSERT_TRUE(swl_rc_isOk(rc), rc, ME, "%s: fail to remove bss %s (%s) rc %d, abort radio removal",
+                    pR->Name, pBss->pAP->alias, apSkname, rc);
+    }
+    SAH_TRACEZ_INFO(ME, "%s: remove iface of bss %s (%s) holding the default connection", pR->Name, pLastBss->pAP->alias,
+                    wld_wpaCtrlInterface_getConnectionSockName(pLastBss->pIface));
+    return s_removeIfaceBySockName(pR, pgIface, pLastBss->pIface);
 }
 
 swl_trl_e wld_rad_hostapd_getCfgParamSupp(T_Radio* pRad, const char* param) {
